From 4b10d789259e634551e00b826284283eb7b0116b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:15:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] T10m: t8_gp uses the current L key and the universal
 key_root

t8_gp chain, cases and omit run the production L of t7_chain (T7c path C,
T10 log tie and onion AIR) in place of its T7-era L copy, which refused unless
T8_GP_OLD_L was set; the copy is removed. t8_gp keys() puts the path C DAG key
leaf after the three chip-set leaves, so gp2, x7 and ladder run under the same
key_root as t7_chain, L, L_Fr and the wrap. t7_chain: path_c() builds the path
C keys (shared with t8_gp); chain, cases_mode, omit, PathC and KEYDAG_IDX are pub.
